{"version":1,"slug":"compound-interest","topic":"What is compound interest?","level":"beginner","title":"How Compound Interest Works","summary":"You will understand how earning interest on your interest makes money grow faster over time.","scopeNote":null,"scenes":[{"id":"intro","kind":"intro","title":"What is compound interest?","segments":[{"id":"intro-0","narration":"Imagine putting one hundred dollars in a jar and watching it quietly double, then double again, all by itself.","sig":"xXbz_MkbNjh7nNwPpoiJNN-8tr5W1CVQ","actions":[{"id":"hero","kind":"icon","cue":"Imagine putting one","text":"Growing money","items":null,"icon":"piggy-bank","at":{"col":0,"row":1,"w":4,"h":4},"from":null,"to":null,"target":null,"color":"blue","expr":null}]},{"id":"intro-1","narration":"Here's our plan. First, Interest on Interest. Then, The Snowball Effect. And finally, Time Is Your Superpower.","sig":"l_qSmTV95PPH156rv4p1c07cIAkj2Q3_","actions":[{"id":"agenda","kind":"list","cue":"Here's our plan","text":null,"items":["Interest on Interest","The Snowball Effect","Time Is Your Superpower"],"icon":null,"at":{"col":5,"row":1,"w":7,"h":4},"from":null,"to":null,"target":null,"color":"blue","expr":null}]}]},{"id":"c1","kind":"chapter","title":"Interest on Interest","segments":[{"id":"c1-0","narration":"Imagine you put money into a piggy bank, and it starts earning interest. Many people think interest is only ever calculated on the original amount you put in.","sig":"luc1HoM7Mf5_gIXmch7yZpAoh3LS5fgO","actions":[{"id":"piggy","kind":"icon","cue":"into a piggy bank","text":"Your Money","items":null,"icon":"piggy-bank","at":{"col":0,"row":0,"w":2,"h":2},"from":null,"to":null,"target":null,"color":"blue","expr":null},{"id":"simple","kind":"box","cue":"only ever calculated","text":"Simple: Original Only","items":null,"icon":null,"at":{"col":4,"row":0,"w":3,"h":2},"from":null,"to":null,"target":null,"color":"red","expr":null},{"id":"a1","kind":"arrow","cue":"only ever calculated","text":null,"items":null,"icon":null,"at":null,"from":"piggy","to":"simple","target":null,"color":null,"expr":null},{"id":"wrong","kind":"text","cue":"original amount","text":"Only original amount","items":null,"icon":null,"at":{"col":8,"row":0,"w":4,"h":1},"from":null,"to":null,"target":null,"color":"red","expr":null}]},{"id":"c1-1","narration":"That is simple interest, and it misses the real magic. Instead, compound interest works like a snowball rolling downhill.","sig":"YdpR1WLmab83xSZcvQxw3JjF47FxU8Q8","actions":[{"id":"x1","kind":"cross_out","cue":"misses the real magic","text":null,"items":null,"icon":null,"at":null,"from":null,"to":null,"target":"wrong","color":"red","expr":null},{"id":"compound","kind":"box","cue":"compound interest works","text":"Compound: Total + Interest","items":null,"icon":null,"at":{"col":4,"row":3,"w":3,"h":2},"from":null,"to":null,"target":null,"color":"green","expr":null},{"id":"snow","kind":"icon","cue":"like a snowball","text":"Snowball","items":null,"icon":"snowflake","at":{"col":0,"row":3,"w":2,"h":2},"from":null,"to":null,"target":null,"color":"blue","expr":null}]},{"id":"c1-2","narration":"As the snowball rolls, it picks up more snow, and your money picks up interest on top of past interest. That is how your savings grow faster and faster.","sig":"Fiamw935P5oQVX7r_OQzC4REaIAxpY8U","actions":[{"id":"a2","kind":"arrow","cue":"picks up more snow","text":"+ grows","items":null,"icon":null,"at":null,"from":"snow","to":"compound","target":null,"color":"green","expr":null},{"id":"t1","kind":"trace","cue":"picks up interest","text":null,"items":null,"icon":"coins","at":null,"from":null,"to":null,"target":"a2","color":"green","expr":null},{"id":"right","kind":"text","cue":"on top of past interest","text":"Interest on interest!","items":null,"icon":null,"at":{"col":8,"row":3,"w":4,"h":1},"from":null,"to":null,"target":null,"color":"green","expr":null},{"id":"c1","kind":"check","cue":"grow faster and faster","text":null,"items":null,"icon":null,"at":null,"from":null,"to":null,"target":"right","color":"green","expr":null}]}]},{"id":"c2","kind":"chapter","title":"The Snowball Effect","segments":[{"id":"c2-0","narration":"Now that you know how the snowball starts, let us watch it roll year by year. Imagine you put one hundred dollars into an account that pays ten percent interest each year.","sig":"nfRyD9Pg5UMGam43Ai9MhXpQcpL5yhcn","actions":[{"id":"start","kind":"icon","cue":"one hundred dollars","text":"Start: $100","items":null,"icon":"coins","at":{"col":0,"row":0,"w":2,"h":2},"from":null,"to":null,"target":null,"color":"blue","expr":null},{"id":"rate","kind":"note","cue":"ten percent interest","text":"10% interest each year","items":null,"icon":null,"at":{"col":3,"row":0,"w":3,"h":2},"from":null,"to":null,"target":null,"color":"purple","expr":null}]},{"id":"c2-1","narration":"In year one, you earn ten dollars, bringing your total to one hundred and ten. In year two, you earn ten percent of that new total, which is eleven dollars.","sig":"xmYsxZFZ8c-HCNA8TzT2U7Tjb_fhn-Iu","actions":[{"id":"years","kind":"flow","cue":"In year one","text":null,"items":["Year 1: $110 (+$10)","Year 2: $121 (+$11)","Year 3: $133.10 (+$12.10)"],"icon":null,"at":{"col":0,"row":2,"w":9,"h":2},"from":null,"to":null,"target":null,"color":"green","expr":null},{"id":"p1","kind":"pulse","cue":"eleven dollars","text":null,"items":null,"icon":null,"at":null,"from":null,"to":null,"target":"years[1]","color":null,"expr":null}]},{"id":"c2-2","narration":"By year three, your interest grows again to twelve dollars and ten cents, pushing your total to one hundred thirty-three dollars and ten cents.","sig":"BJE-9AR-TK5p4iX4M-W9rhVDp6Pk89aO","actions":[{"id":"t1","kind":"trace","cue":"By year three","text":null,"items":null,"icon":"coins","at":null,"from":null,"to":null,"target":"years","color":"green","expr":null},{"id":"final","kind":"number","cue":"one hundred thirty-three","text":"$133.10","items":["After 3 years"],"icon":null,"at":{"col":9,"row":2,"w":3,"h":2},"from":null,"to":null,"target":null,"color":"green","expr":null},{"id":"p2","kind":"pulse","cue":"ten cents","text":null,"items":null,"icon":null,"at":null,"from":null,"to":null,"target":"final","color":null,"expr":null}]}]},{"id":"c3","kind":"chapter","title":"Time Is Your Superpower","segments":[{"id":"c3-0","narration":"Now that you have seen the snowball effect in action, let us look at what happens when you give it time. Imagine you put in one hundred dollars at ten percent interest and just leave it alone.","sig":"mGqLhz5PZevR_1KVEfeE2GBrn2gjhA2o","actions":[{"id":"start","kind":"box","cue":"one hundred dollars","text":"$100 at 10%","items":null,"icon":null,"at":{"col":0,"row":0,"w":3,"h":2},"from":null,"to":null,"target":null,"color":"blue","expr":null}]},{"id":"c3-1","narration":"After one year, you have one hundred and ten dollars. After ten years, it is two hundred and fifty-nine dollars, and after twenty years, it jumps to six hundred and seventy-three dollars!","sig":"Vwv_G2CDwGOUdL-DLk5GBh8-qjwDDQeD","actions":[{"id":"growth","kind":"bars","cue":"After one year","text":null,"items":["1 Year: $110","10 Years: $259","20 Years: $673"],"icon":null,"at":{"col":4,"row":0,"w":7,"h":4},"from":null,"to":null,"target":null,"color":"green","expr":null},{"id":"a1","kind":"arrow","cue":"After one year","text":null,"items":null,"icon":null,"at":null,"from":"start","to":"growth","target":null,"color":null,"expr":null},{"id":"p1","kind":"pulse","cue":"six hundred and seventy-three","text":null,"items":null,"icon":null,"at":null,"from":null,"to":null,"target":"growth","color":"green","expr":null}]},{"id":"c3-2","narration":"You did not add a single extra dollar, yet your money multiplied more than six times. That is why starting early is your real superpower.","sig":"sYQG_P_sT1i5Wtl5s_BgGhIVxdsSSkfF","actions":[{"id":"power","kind":"note","cue":"starting early","text":"Time multiplies your money!","items":null,"icon":null,"at":{"col":0,"row":3,"w":3,"h":2},"from":null,"to":null,"target":null,"color":"purple","expr":null},{"id":"h1","kind":"highlight","cue":"real superpower","text":null,"items":null,"icon":null,"at":null,"from":null,"to":null,"target":"power","color":null,"expr":null}]}]},{"id":"recap","kind":"recap","title":"Recap","segments":[{"id":"recap-0","narration":"So remember: compound interest pays interest on past interest, your money grows like a snowball, and starting early gives time its superpower. What questions do you have?","sig":"Oxx5v04B-eoj3hTBDs3fnS2oJwVKHLl5","actions":[{"id":"recap_list","kind":"list","cue":"So remember: compound interest","text":null,"items":["Interest on past interest","Grows like a snowball","Starting early multiplies savings"],"icon":null,"at":{"col":1,"row":1,"w":6,"h":4},"from":null,"to":null,"target":null,"color":"ink","expr":null},{"id":"recap_icon","kind":"icon","cue":"gives time its superpower","text":"Start Early","items":null,"icon":"trending-up","at":{"col":8,"row":2,"w":2,"h":2},"from":null,"to":null,"target":null,"color":"green","expr":null}]}]}],"quiz":[{"question":"What makes compound interest different from simple interest?","options":["It only pays on your first deposit","It pays interest on past interest","It requires adding money every month","It never changes from year to year"],"answer":1,"explanation":"Compound interest calculates new interest on both your original money and the interest you already earned.","chapter":1},{"question":"If you have 110 dollars and earn 10 percent interest, how much interest do you earn that year?","options":["10 dollars","12 dollars","11 dollars","100 dollars"],"answer":2,"explanation":"Ten percent of 110 dollars is 11 dollars, which is more than the 10 dollars you earned in year one.","chapter":2},{"question":"Why is starting early so powerful for compound interest?","options":["Time gives the snowball more years to grow","Banks pay higher rates to younger people","You only pay interest at the very end","Money doubles every single month"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Giving your money more years lets the snowball effect multiply your savings without adding extra cash.","chapter":3}],"suggestions":["How inflation affects your savings","Simple vs compound interest","How credit card interest works"],"models":{"lesson":"google/gemini-4-hydrogen","voice":"google/gemini-3.8-flash-tts"},"createdAt":"2026-11-17T12:46:43.351Z","audioBase":"/samples/compound-interest"}